{
	"_doc": [
		"Keys are Terraria internal NPC names (NPCID). sprite: NPC_<n> sheet; frames are stacked vertically.",
		"size: world-space [width, height] in blocks. ai: slime | fighter | flyer | bat | harpy | swim | turret | snatcher | boss_eoc | caster (Terraria's AI_008, the Goblin Sorcerer: teleports near you every 650 ticks, then casts its \"cast\" shot {projectile, speed, damage} three times).",
		"invasion: one of the Goblin Army's goblins (spawned by it, counted toward its defeat: invasion_points, default 1). shoot.sight: shoots only with a clear line to you (the Goblin Archer).",
		"swim: lives in water (chases you while you swim, wanders otherwise, flops when stranded); pulse: moves in jellyfish pushes; glow_frames: [first, last] shown when you are close. floats: a town NPC afloat at the surface (the Sleeping Angler).",
		"critter: Terraria's critters (scripts/entities/npc.gd, Critters section): harmless, 5 life, caught with a Bug Net as their \"catch\" item (released again by using it). ai critter_walk (aiStyle 7: idle and wander, walk_frames, speed px a tick, faster hurt), bird (24: sits till you're near, then flies off: fly_frames, sit_frame), firefly (64: drifts, glows at night or underground: light), butterfly (65: flutters, flees; variants: the Butterfly's 8 colours, each its own catch), crawler (66: worms and grubs, speed), snail (67), duck (68 with 7: walks, swims on the surface, flies off), hopper (1: the grasshopper's hops), swim with passive: a fish that only wanders (goldfish). gold: a gold critter. lava_bait: an Underworld critter: a plain Bug Net catching it burns you.",
		"shoot: {projectile, interval s, speed, damage, range, gravity} - hostile shots at the player (any AI).",
		"turret: stays put and shoots (antlions). snatcher: lunges at you on a vine from where it spawned (tether blocks). upright: a flier that flips instead of turning with its flight.",
		"sprite_angle: degrees to turn a flier so its art points along its motion (0 = art points down, like the Eater of Souls; the Demon Eye looks sideways: 90).",
		"tint multiplies the sprite (Terraria recolours one slime sprite for every slime).",
		"trim_bottom: pixels cut off the bottom of each frame (guide lines in some sheets).",
		"walk_frames / fly_frames: [first, last] frame of the walk / wing cycle (default: all frames).",
		"drops: [item, min, max, chance]. drops_one_of: one of these, always.",
		"king_slime: Terraria's King Slime (AI_015_KingSlime): hops at you in a cycle (one a big jump), shrinking as it's hurt, teleporting next to you when it can't reach you, spitting out Blue Slimes as it loses life.",
		"worm: Terraria's worms (AI_006_Worms): a head drags its segments (worm.kinds) through the ground; speed / accel in px/tick, spacing in px; killing a middle segment splits it in two. sprite_ppb: draw the sheet at this many texture pixels a block (its true size). boss_group: one boss made of several NPCs (its bar sums them; the last to die drops boss_drops). spawner: false keeps it out of the test world's spawners.",
		"image: an Images/ sheet that isn't an NPC_<n> one (instead of sprite). part: not a creature, a piece drawn by another (Skeletron's arm bones: skeletron_arm, its art pointing down each bone); it's here so the NPC picker can give it a 3D or rendered look. name: its name where Terraria has none.",
		"night_buttons: chat buttons only at night (the Old Man's Curse, which brings Skeletron).",
		"xray: shown through the blocks in front of it, dimmed and tinted (bosses always are: Terraria draws NPCs in front of the tiles); head_icon: its Terraria boss head icon (NPC_Head_Boss_<n>), shown at the screen's edge pointing to it when it's out of view.",
		"brain: Terraria's Brain of Cthulhu (aiStyle 54): brings its Creepers (ai creeper, aiStyle 55: they circle it and now and then charge at you) and can't be hurt while any are left; it drifts at you, fading out and back in somewhere near you now and then. With them gone it sheds its outer brain and comes at you, teleporting close by often. Out of the Crimson (or with you dead) it sinks away. bar_adds: [kind, count] whose life the boss bar adds to its own (its Creepers).",
		"queen_bee: Terraria's Queen Bee (aiStyle 43): in turn charges at you (lining up level with you, then dashing past), hovers over you sending out bees (Bee / BeeSmall, ai bee: aiStyle 5's homing), and hovers higher shooting stingers; faster and fiercer above the surface or out of the Jungle. music: its boss music (a MusicID name; default Boss1). drops_chain entries may be [[one of these items], chance].",
		"skeletron: Terraria's Skeletron head (aiStyle 11): brings its two hands (skeletron_hand, aiStyle 12), hovers over you, every 800 ticks spins at you for 400 (its defense 10 lower); enraged by day (9999 damage and defense, spinning at you fast); the Dungeon Guardian is one always enraged. drops_chain: [item, chance] tried in order, the first that rolls drops (one of them at most).",
		"knockback_resist: Terraria's knockBackResist, how much of a hit's knockback it takes (1 all, 0 none). flight: a flier's Terraria steering, in px/tick (a block is 24 px, a tick 1/60 s): x / y [acceleration toward you, extra braking while moving away (negative: less), braking above top speed, top speed] (AI_002 eyes, aiStyle 14 bats), or homing [speed, acceleration] (AI_005: flies at you, accelerating twice as hard against its motion).",
		"town: a Terraria town NPC that moves into a house (scripts/entities/town.gd). arrives: what brings them (none: from the start; money: 50 silver on you; life: the Merchant lives here and you've more than 100 max life; gun: a gun or bullets on you; boss: a boss defeated; explosive: an explosive on you; freed / woken: the Bound Goblin freed, the Sleeping Angler woken). shop: items sold at their value (an entry [item, \"night\"] only at night); buttons: chat buttons besides Shop and Close (Help, Heal, Status)."
	],
